<title>HONG KONG: GE unit wins HK$93.6 mln HK airport deal.</title>
<headline>GE unit wins HK$93.6 mln HK airport deal.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Hong Kong Airport Authority said in a statement it awarded on Friday a HK$93.6 million contract for traffic control and surveillance systems to General Electric Co unit General Electric Corp (Hong Kong) Ltd.</p>
<p>The contract includes the design, supply and installation of a traffic control and surveillance system for the landslide road network at the new airport at Chek Lap Kok, it said.</p>
<p>The project will have a construction and installation period of 14 months, and General Electric Corp (Hong Kong) will also provide comprehensive maintenance of the system during a 12-month warranty period, the statement said.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6590</p>
</text>
